// Title: Diskshadow Script Mode Execution
// Sigma ID: 0c2f8629-7129-4a8a-9897-7e0768f13ff2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Ivan Dyachkov, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-07 | Modified: 2024-03-13
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218, execution
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects execution of "Diskshadow.exe" in script mode using the "/s" flag. Attackers often abuse
//   "diskshadow" to execute scripts that deleted the shadow copies on the systems. Investigate the
//   content of the scripts and its location.
// False positives:
//   - Likely from legitimate backup scripts
// References:
//   - https://bohops.com/2018/03/26/diskshadow-the-return-of-vss-evasion-persistence-and-active-directory-database-extraction/
//   - https://www.ired.team/offensive-security/credential-access-and-credential-dumping/ntds.dit-enumeration
//   - https://medium.com/@cyberjyot/lolbin-execution-via-diskshadow-f6ff681a27a4
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/diskshadow
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_diskshadow_script_mode.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "diskshadow.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\diskshadow.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-s " or ProcessCommandLine contains "/s " or ProcessCommandLine contains "–s " or ProcessCommandLine contains "—s " or ProcessCommandLine contains "―s ")
